rust-proxmox-daemon (1.0.1-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * reap the intermediate process of a reload before announcing the new main
    process to systemd. If it had not exited yet, systemd did not supervise the
    new process as its own child, could not collect its exit status, and for
    units with KillMode=mixed killed the service with SIGKILL on stop instead
    of sending SIGTERM first.

  * keep a shutdown or reload request made before the daemon starts waiting for
    one, for example a SIGHUP right after startup. Such a request got lost, and
    the daemon then no longer reacted to any further SIGINT or SIGHUP.

 -- Proxmox Support Team <support@proxmox.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:58:28 +0100

